{
  "id": "common-region",
  "term": "common region",
  "definition": "Common region is an extrinsic perceptual grouping factor in which separate visual elements are enclosed within the same surrounding area, leading them to be perceived more as a group. In the cited study, placing targets within a single shared mask increased how often they disappeared and reappeared together, without changing overall disappearance time.",
